 ## [Unreleased]
 
+### Added
+
+- `ToolRegistry.execute` now validates `input` against each tool's declared `inputSchema` (JSON Schema, via `ajv`) before invoking the executor. A call with missing required properties, wrong-typed fields, or enum violations returns a `ToolResponse` describing what failed — the executor is not invoked, and the rejection text is fed back to the model as a `tool_result` so it can correct the call within the existing tool-round budget. Invalid values are never echoed in rejection messages or log lines. Static tool schemas are compiled once at `register` time (a broken schema throws immediately, naming the tool); function-valued sources compile per distinct returned schema, cached by object reference. Extra properties pass through to the executor unchanged.
+
